# 114: 421+HP (Lightning Sword) on the SEPARATED (CPS-2 WIDE) wheel — the
# WIDE-track twin of replay 48 (GitHub #114, 14z-127).
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. Replay 48's P1 path (U,U,R from the default Demitri cell)
# walks to slot 0x0F, which is Donovan ONLY on the SUBSTITUTED stock track.
# Since the 14z-115 select-wheel separation the tenants live on their own
# appended row, so on a WIDE build that same path lands on JEDAH — measured
# 2026-09-02: P1 +0x60 = 0x000b0d2e (jedah) on merged-m14, and the move that
# gets measured is Jedah's 421+HP (3 hits / 11 damage, victim pushed
# 728 -> 852). That artefact is what GitHub #114 mistook for a Donovan
# regression. A tenant replay is only a claim about the build it was
# authored for ([VSP-156]).
#
# This script uses the APPENDED-CELL path of replay 36 (L,L,D,D -> cell 0x13)
# and is otherwise replay 48 frame for frame. BUILD-ONLY: on a stock or
# vanilla set the final D lands elsewhere and the run is meaningless — the
# gate asserts P1's identity against tests/expected/roster_pairings/bases.tsv
# rather than trusting the path.
#
# Measured on merged-m14 (build/m3b_merged21, vsavjw): P1 +0x60 = 0x003fa9d0
# (donovan), 6 hits / 10 total at f2638/2648/2659/2669/2680/2690, victim HELD
# at x=728 until the shake ends — identical to the stock twin and matching
# native vsav2's 6 hits / 10 total (replay 51).
